c Random Instance of Urquhart's Problem for SAT (size=6).
c Like Hole, this problem as been proved to be exponential for resolution.
c N.B. : instance is unsatisfiable by construction.
c
c Come from the paper 'Hard Examples for Resolution'.
c        Source : Laurent Simon, simon@lri.fr. May 1999.
c
c n=6, so there is m^2=36 vertices in each part of the bipartite graph.
c Bases creations :
c   - a '1' charge is 'there must be an even number of negated vars'
c   - edges contains variables from which all subbases are constructed.
c vertex A0 :(charge=1), (edges=[133,125])
c vertex A1 :(charge=1), (edges=[135,168,77,155,159,125,147])
c vertex A2 :(charge=0), (edges=[34,69,109,147,101])
c vertex A3 :(charge=0), (edges=[26,105,90,101,70])
c vertex A4 :(charge=0), (edges=[85,70,113])
c vertex A5 :(charge=1), (edges=[170,18,146,174,113,156])
c vertex A6 :(charge=1), (edges=[138,143,58,172,15,156,91])
c vertex A7 :(charge=0), (edges=[108,92,142,42,91,79])
c vertex A8 :(charge=0), (edges=[19,178,83,68,80,79,72])
c vertex A9 :(charge=0), (edges=[102,8,160,72,47])
c vertex A10 :(charge=0), (edges=[43,47,115])
c vertex A11 :(charge=1), (edges=[103,177,97,139,21,115,16])
c vertex A12 :(charge=1), (edges=[129,67,16,78])
c vertex A13 :(charge=0), (edges=[124,157,78,40])
c vertex A14 :(charge=1), (edges=[46,134,40,62])
c vertex A15 :(charge=0), (edges=[117,130,162,81,154,62,158])
c vertex A16 :(charge=1), (edges=[148,163,93,158,152])
c vertex A17 :(charge=0), (edges=[12,45,28,152,127])
